{
 "brief": "Amjad Obeidat, a Palestinian prisoner held in Israeli jails, has entered his 23rd year in captivity as he faces repeated solitary confinement and restrictions on family visits, Shehab Wire reported. His family has been barred from seeing him, and contact with him has been severed since April.\n\nThe long-term detainee's conditions reflect broader concerns about the treatment of Palestinian prisoners held in Israeli facilities, where isolation and limited family access remain persistent practices.",
